Well, i too have had a couple ideas for the game that
in my opion would make the game more enjoyable/fair.

First off, I agree that it is a pain to have a stack
of one or two objects inventoried every time I walk over
it.  And that certain commands like pickup, should be 
fixed, but since every other post in recent history has
addressed these points, I shall not.

Monsters:

To start off with, monsters in the stronghold, and in 
Hell, should be made a little harder.  I seems that by
the time that I make it to Vllade, he is a total whimp.
The only creature that even thinks about bringing fear
to my characters is the minitor, because he is the only
one that will cause more than 20 points of damage in
battle.

Magic:

I don't understand why a character should lose his 
spells from casting them.  Although I do believe that
either the number of points it costs to cast the spell
should be increased, or the number of spell points a 
character has should be decreased.

Just because a first level character knows the spell
fireball, should not mean that he can cast it with
100% reliability.  There should be a % chance of spell
failure becuase the spell was too powerfull.

Certain spells should be made area effect.  Such as
fireball and sleep.  And yes, this includes if the caster
gets hit by the explosion, he should be taking damage.

Resistance:

Should not be a all or now proposition.  Just because 
a character eats a winter wolf, he shouldn't for then
on take no damage from cold.  Maybe set up a percental
associated with each resistance, that will slowly 
increase with level, or with eating certain creatures,
so that a cold attack still either has a chance at
full damage, or even if a character is 25% cold resistance,
then he only takes 75% damage.  etc...

Neat items:

ring of conflict:  monsters who have this on them, should
affect the player.  The player can not attack the creature
with a ring of conflict while a monster is adjacent to him.

amulet of peace:  cancles the effect of a ring of conflict.
can be worn by either a monster (affecting all monsters in 
the room) or by the player.  
At first I thought it should be called a peace button, but
there is not an armor class called button right now.  So maybe
it should be an amulet, so that if the player wears the AoP,
he cannot wear an AoLS.

Sunglasses:  A new helmet.  uncursed prevents blinding from 
bright lights, blessed prevents all blindings, and cursed ones
are just too dark, and causes blindness.

Trenchcoat:  A new cloak.  contains a bag (pockects).  Blessed
trenchcoats would act like bags of holding.  Maybe the healer
would start out with one of these.

I have a few more ideas, but I am currently
five minutes late to class.  I will get back to yall
with more, if these ideas are liked.  :)


